    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0359" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/990½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I am sending you the
                    telegram drafted by Mr. Lansing.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d248-f1"/> I have just
                    had time to read it but not time to go over it with a view to digesting it
                    sentence by sentence. He has worked in nearly, if not all of your language but
                    the impression it makes upon me is that the tone of it is a little more severe
                    than the tone of your memorandum.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d248-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>If, after you have had an opportunity to consider it, you desire any exchange of
                    views I am at your service, as is Mr. Lansing.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d248-f1" n="61" xml:id="d248-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for the telegram as sent, see <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_152">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1915, supp., p.
                    152</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d248-f2" n="62" xml:id="d248-f2-content">
                <p>Enclosure to President Wilson’s letter of Mar. 19, 1915, <ref target="#pg278">p.
                        278</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
